{%# admin => { templates => 'root/queue' }

     This directory is a template root searched BEFORE the bundled one,
     one name at a time - so it holds exactly the template it changes
     (this one), and overview/jobs/workers/locks/crons/layout all keep
     coming from the dist. Upgrade Punk::Queue and the six you did not
     touch move with it.

     Which root serves which name is decided at registration, so a
     misspelled filename here is a boot croak, not a page that silently
     stays ours.

     Every template renders with: prefix, title, page, version, live,
     csrf_cookie, nav, styles, scripts (and id, on the job page). The
     layout also gets `content`.
%}
<h1 class="page-title">Overview</h1>

<div class="pq-panel pq-mailer-note">
  <strong>Punk Mailer</strong> - this UI is mounted inside the application
  at <code>{% prefix %}</code>, behind the same guard stack as the rest of
  it. <a href="/">Back to the app</a>.
</div>

<div class="pq-panel">
  <div id="pqStats" class="stats-bar stats-bar-stretch"></div>
</div>
<div class="pq-panel">
  <h2>Last 24 hours</h2>
  <div id="pqHistory"></div>
</div>
<div class="pq-panel pq-detail">
  <dl>
    <dt>Schema version</dt><dd id="pqSchema">-</dd>
    <dt>Workers alive</dt><dd id="pqWorkersAlive">-</dd>
    <dt>Lifetime enqueued</dt><dd id="pqEnqueued">-</dd>
    <dt>punk-queue</dt><dd>{% version %}</dd>
  </dl>
</div>
